{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d1f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0789a-315e-7c93-91ec-e79f4e2ce50f"},"sequence":1876,"recorded_at":1780531400003747,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"884b6426-fd25-4492-8e5c-d502ad4c11cd"},"task_id":"884b6426-fd25-4492-8e5c-d502ad4c11cd","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"884b6426-fd25-4492-8e5c-d502ad4c11cd","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 28-32\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-// owner gate below. The decoder half of that agreement is pinned by the\n-// derived TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON sweep,\n-// which judges escape and raw-UTF-8 vectors through the shared\n-// decodeStrictObject every entry here reads through, and any shape-rule\n-// change must land in both validators in the same change.\n+// owner gate below. The decoder half of that agreement is pinned by the\n+// derived TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON sweep,\n+// which judges escape and raw-UTF-8 vectors through the shared\n+// decodeStrictObject every entry here reads through, and any shape-rule\n+// change must land in both validators in the same change.\n+//\n+// Binding verification split, stated plainly: the three terminal\n+// schemas verify their identity binding — terminalbackend's Parse\n+// entries recompute the omit-self digest and refuse a mismatched claim\n+// — while provider-identity records admitted here do not. CheckIdentity\n+// requires record_id to be a well-formed digest but never recomputes\n+// it, and the conjoined CalculateObjectIdentity entry validates shape\n+// only; the entry that would attest the binding,\n+// canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity, is not consulted. The reason is\n+// transport scope, not oversight: this gate validates a record embedded\n+// in a request-correlated provider response (request_id match plus the\n+// wantProviderID caller correlation above), and it must admit the\n+// pinned Section 5.5 example itself, whose record_id is illustrative\n+// rather than the true omit-self digest. Binding attestation belongs to\n+// the identity owner at the persistence layer, through VerifyObjectIdentity.\n"}}}
