{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dc93","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0789a-315e-7c93-91ec-e79f4e2ce50f"},"sequence":3236,"recorded_at":1780531400006467,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"5992999e-afa7-43f5-9ca2-6ee7a0a6cba4"},"task_id":"5992999e-afa7-43f5-9ca2-6ee7a0a6cba4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"5992999e-afa7-43f5-9ca2-6ee7a0a6cba4","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-133-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ...; git log --oneline -2 -- LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook convention\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 2249 — CI gates leaf round 2: five review findings closed, all claims reproduce\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk rework (review-verdict-rev1, F1–F5 blocking + verb-battery observation). `internal/cigate` + `.github/workflows/ci.yml` + README. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched (restored byte-identical after two probe mutants; `git status` clean on both).\\n- F1: deleted the `Record live probe verdicts` step — it ran a synthetic-verdict test and grepped a constant line through a non-gating pipe. CI now scans the README with every probe forced unavailable (stronger than live scanning, host-independent); README table and `cigate/doc.go` say so, and the workflow comment states `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site.\\n- F3: wired, not deleted. New `TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation` holds `go test -list ^Fuzz` output equal to `FuzzTargets()`; CI's fuzz-smoke runs it name-guarded before smoking. Entry-drop mutant kills both the derivation test and `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction`.\\n- F5: fuzz-smoke now derives per package over `secconftest` + `canonicaljson` + `scalar` (8+4+1=13, count pinned), each smoked with the `^fuzz: elapsed` guard — all 13 observed locally. `doc.go` no longer claims entry points stay in one package.\\n- F4: backtick bound stated in `doc.go` Stated bounds and the README row, pinned by `TestUnbacktickedProseIsOutsideTheScanner` (bare-prose positive claims admitted). Backtick-widening mutant killed by that test and by the real-README gate (bare `fifo` in prose gets refused).\\n- BATTERY: verb/negation size `Fatalf`s replaced by per-row behavioural kills + `battery-covers-gate` censuses. Three rewritten negation rows (`n't`, `pending`, `unless`) each previously hid behind a second negation. Censused drops: 5/5 verbs and 13/13 negations kill in their own subtest (spot-verified `supported`, `pending`; `available` also trips `TestFindingCarriesLine` by shared sentence).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` rev2 (11/11 AC rows, 30-mutant battery, per-job red proofs) + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_mutants-rev2.log` + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_verify-rev2.log`. Full suite 22 ok, `-race` 22 ok, `-cover` 22 lines (cigate 90.5%), vet both GOOS, gofmt, catalog freshness, `tracecheck` all exit 0.\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not fixed here): catalog-freshness step defeated by `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` (token preserved); at HEAD before this leaf. The contract-version gate still catches version drift with the directive disarmed.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2248 — CI gates leaf: cigate library, ten-job workflow, no new main\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk (final leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New `internal/cigate` (doc/contracts/claims/targets + 3 test files, no `main`); `.github/workflows/ci.yml` 1 job → 10; README \\\"Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\\\" section. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched; no foreign guard weakened.\\n- DECISION: no new `main` package. First Rosewood `cmd/cigate` tripped `TestEmbeddedDocumentNeverReachesAProductBinary` + `TestModuleHasNoProductCommandYet` (lib reaches specdoc via secconftest). Widening that allowlist would self-mint an exemption, so the command was deleted; CI drives gates through focused name-guarded `go test -run` selections instead. Recorded in `internal/cigate/doc.go`.\\n- FINDING: `go test -fuzz='^NoSuch$'` exits 0 (\\\"no fuzz tests to fuzz\\\"). Fuzz-smoke step therefore requires the `^fuzz: elapsed` line per target, proven both directions (real 0, bogus 1).\\n- FINDING: existing `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` pins four literals in ci.yml; the rewrite initially dropped `go build ./...` and used non-verbose test. Restored: native Build step + `go test ./... -v -count=1`. The guard worked as designed.\\n- FINDING: N3-v1 mutant (drop one marker) survived — marker arm has redundancy by construction, not a hole. Replaced with boundary-anchoring narrowing (substring match), killed by new `TestSubstringIsNotAMarker`.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` (11/11 AC rows, 13-row mutant table, per-job red proofs with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_mutants.log`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race ./...` exit 0 (22 ok x3 sweeps), `-cover` exit 0 (22 lines, cigate 90.5%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (60/55 contracts, unchanged). Mutants 13 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL, 11 killed (5 narrowing + 6 arm-deletion), 2 census survivors with bounds (order-only).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2155 — secconftest round-3 rework: crashed commit counts as committed, Require wiring pinned, LOGBOOK corrected\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830