{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dcff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0789a-315e-7c93-91ec-e79f4e2ce50f"},"sequence":3290,"recorded_at":1780531400006575,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"991286c9-5106-4a42-ba8b-579d37a173bb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"58740d1f-0f9c-49af-afba-054cd7e93f42"},"task_id":"58740d1f-0f9c-49af-afba-054cd7e93f42","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"58740d1f-0f9c-49af-afba-054cd7e93f42","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-06\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 2250 — v3 envelope owner named (terminalbackend), provider error lift built\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y (second leaf of STORY-260905-3t31e9; advisories A3/A4 + carried F3). New: `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (closed §7.A descriptor parse + `AdmitProviderDescriptor`), `provider/lift.go` (`Lift`); edited: provhost protocol/doc/identity comments + derived error contract, provider doc, 7.A registry group + digest, terminalbackend inventory rows. Leaf-1 production untouched.\n+- DECISION: §7.A owner is terminalbackend, not provhost. Provhost cannot admit 3.0.0 transport: our host writes v2 requests and §7.A sends v2/v3 mismatches down the §15.1 close/termination rule, so admission would trust a foreign major and redden the pinned `3.0.0 → incompatible_protocol` gates. Refusal is the specified outcome; the dual-stack host (v3 requests + descriptor carriage + 1.3.0 decode) is a follow-up specified in the outcome, not a silent scope.\n+- DECISION: `provider.Error` keeps machine-local facts for logs; the wire message is rebuilt from the stable code alone by `Lift` (static text, empty details, cause local-only). Constructor restructuring would not remove the rebuild need, so the seam is the lift, documented in `provider/doc.go`.\n+- FINDING: `git stash create -u` trees omit untracked files — verify candidate trees with `git ls-tree`. The recorded tree OID was built via a detached index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE` copy + `add -A` + `write-tree`) with blob hashes checked against worktree bytes.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` (11/11 AC rows with call sites, 19-row mutant table, gates with exit codes). Tree `fe043ab07a847b5a257f60f6c3b93295d19b6e50`.\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, catalog current, `tracecheck` ok. Battery 17 applied / 17 killed / 0 survivors (+ NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls). Fuzz smoke not run (targets in untouched packages; CI runs it).\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n"}}}
